  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the MMSE (Mini-Mental State Examination) grader. VERIFIED QUIRK: the AssessmentData type carries BOTH a languageScores.naming1/naming2 pair AND a repetitionCommands object with its own naming1/naming2 - the grader (calculateMMSE) and domainBreakdown read ONLY repetitionCommands for every language item, including naming; languageScores.naming1/naming2 are a UI-only field that form-app.js bridges into repetitionCommands before grading, so a persona's state must set repetitionCommands directly (languageScores is populated too here, for realism, but is never read by the grader). Only items scored exactly 1 (correct) appear in firedRules; a 0 (incorrect, actively answered) and null (unanswered) both contribute 0 points and are both absent from firedRules - so an all-zero submission grades 0/30 with an EMPTY firedRules array, even though every item was actually answered. detectAdditionalFlags(state) is a split engine (form-app.js calls it as detectAdditionalFlags(state)) whose domain-answered checks (recallAnswered, regAnswered, langAnswered, attAnswered) DO distinguish 0 from null - a domain scored all-0 still counts as 'answered' and can fire its flag, but a domain left entirely null cannot. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas cognitive-assessment --update",
